vtpm-mds (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Split the source into two binary packages: vtpm-mds (hypervisor daemon,
    legacy aliases prox-mds and qemu-mds, systemd unit, /etc/vtpm-mds
    config and /var/lib/vtpm-mds state) and devid-enroll (guest DevID
    enrollment client and its man page only).
  * BREAKING: upgrading vtpm-mds no longer leaves /usr/bin/devid-enroll on
    the host. Guests install devid-enroll_*.deb instead; hypervisors keep
    installing vtpm-mds_*.deb only.
  * devid-enroll declares Breaks/Replaces: vtpm-mds (<< 0.2.0) so the move
    of /usr/bin/devid-enroll off the host package unpacks cleanly. Neither
    package depends on or recommends the other.
  * devid-enroll installs no systemd unit and no IMDS listener, so it is
    safe to install inside guest images.

 -- Andreas Dembach <andreas.dembach@dg-i.net>  Sun, 20 Sep 2026 12:15:57 +0200

vtpm-mds (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial Debian packaging. debian/ was referenced by `make deb` /
    dpkg-buildpackage but never committed; this restores a native package
    with a systemd unit and Proxmox-oriented install layout.
  * Install /usr/sbin/vtpm-mds (aliases prox-mds, qemu-mds),
    /usr/bin/devid-enroll, /etc/vtpm-mds/config.yaml (listen
    169.254.169.1:80, Proxmox /etc/pve inventory, host swTPM PKI paths),
    and /lib/systemd/system/vtpm-mds.service.

 -- Andreas Dembach <andreas.dembach@dg-i.net>  Sat, 12 Sep 2026 08:47:00 +0000
